---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import OutsideList from '../components/OutsideList.astro';
import { confidence } from '../data/confidence.js';

// Outside help. It opens normally, in the same tab; the list says once that outside sites may contain spoilers.
// This page says nothing about what any outside site does. The map links live on the Places page, shown once Places is on.
const outside = [{ href: 'https://support.rockstargames.com', title: 'Rockstar Support', about: "Rockstar's own support site." }];
---

<Base title="About" description="How this guide handles spoilers and sources, and who it is not.">
  <h1>About this guide</h1>

  <div class="prose">
    <h2>Spoilers</h2>
    <p>
      The guide has one spoiler dial at the top of every screen. It starts on Off, and each step adds more:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Off.</strong> The basics: setup, install, settings, controls, saving and fixes, plus what is and is not in the game at launch. For example, how to save, or what to do when the game crashes.</li>
      <li><strong>Places.</strong> Adds where things are. For example, a map of what is where.</li>
      <li><strong>Mild.</strong> Adds how the game's systems work in play: what they are called, what they cost, how they respond, and tips from people who have played. For example, how one of the game's systems behaves once you are in it.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Off names a game system only to say it exists; where you could lose something, Off says so and one tap shows how to avoid it.
    </p>
    <p>
      There is no story at any setting.
    </p>
    <p>
      Hidden text is not in the pages you load at the default setting. It sits in separate files. At Off the
      app fetches none of them, except a single detail when you tap to show it. When you raise the level, the app
      downloads that level's files in the background: its search file, the list of outside map sites and its answer
      pages, so search finds them at once and they open offline. Lowering the level removes them from this device.
      An answer with a hidden detail says so, for example
      "1 mild detail hidden", and you tap to show it. Showing one detail does not change the dial. A detail you chose to show stays saved on this device for offline use until you lower the level or clear this site's data.
    </p>

    <h2>Where facts come from</h2>
    <p>
      Every answer links to its sources and shows the date we last checked them. We restate facts in our
      own words. Each answer also says how sure we are:
    </p>
    <ul>
      {Object.values(confidence).map((c) => <li><strong>{c.label}, {c.short}.</strong> {c.text}</li>)}
    </ul>
    <p>If we could not find a source, there is no answer. We do not guess.</p>

    <h2>Maps and help</h2>
    <p>
      Outside map sites exist, and this guide does not rebuild them. Their links appear on the <a href="/places/">Places page</a> once
      the spoiler setting is Places or higher. At Off no map link is shown.
    </p>
    <p>For help from the publisher:</p>
  </div>
  <div class="links"><OutsideList links={outside} /></div>

  <div class="prose">
    <h2>Unofficial</h2>
    <p>
      This is an unofficial fan project. It is not affiliated with or endorsed by Rockstar Games or
      Take-Two Interactive. It uses no Rockstar logos, art or fonts.
    </p>

    <h2>Your progress and privacy</h2>
    <p>
      Nothing here is tracked: no analytics, no ads, no accounts. The only cookies are the sign-in cookie that
      lets you past the password page and a spoiler-level cookie (<code>lfg_dial</code>) that holds just the word off, places or mild.
      Your spoiler setting stays on this device, and its level is also sent to this site in that cookie so the server can
      refuse hidden pages; the server reads it on each request and keeps nothing, so it is not stored there or tied to a person.
    </p>
    <p>
      This device keeps your settings and ticks in the browser's storage. It also keeps a copy of the guide's
      pages, so they work offline. Turning the spoiler setting down removes the hidden pages from that copy.
    </p>
    <p>
      When syncing works, your ticked to-dos are copied to this site's own private store, so they follow
      you from one device to another. Nothing else is sent. The <a href="/checklist/">Checklist</a> says whether the last sync worked:
      if it did not, your ticks stay saved on this device and we try again. Your spoiler setting,
      console, theme and stage are never copied to the store, so every new device starts with spoilers off.
    </p>
    <p>
      On the <a href="/checklist/">Checklist</a> screen you can also copy your ticks as a code and paste it into another device. The
      code is only text and holds ticks only. Copying it sends it nowhere by itself.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .prose { max-inline-size: 40rem; }
  .prose h2 { margin-block: var(--space-5) var(--space-2); }
  .prose p, .prose ul { margin-block: 0 var(--space-3); }
  .prose ul { padding-inline-start: var(--space-5); display: grid; gap: var(--space-2); }
  .links { max-inline-size: 40rem; margin-block-end: var(--space-3); }
</style>
